ecodable intent that must survive the prune, a candidate pushed only under a wrong ref that must survive it, and case 9's digest mismatch now asserts an ordinary parenting line rather than a record that parents nothing.\n\nF3, implementation status overclaiming the bootstrap case. Closed. Case 4's first run no longer calls itself the run that works today. Its oracle is computable now - the bootstrap profile's object id follows from the genesis hash and needs no fold change - and its run is not, because a batch resolving to that profile needs a drain, an entry carrying a profile header, and the auditor's contract-version lookup, none of which exist; so every assertion after the object id is design-only, the reproduction of the two refusal reasons included. The block's closing sentence now says every run in it is blocked, the first included. The bootstrap paragraph in the profile section says what the object buys today is an oracle and not a run. The measured-and-not-measured paragraph adds the tier-1 drain to the list of obligations. And the spike summary now opens by saying no case in the list has been executed, because the tier-1 drain does not exist, with measured Git and forge premises marked as premises rather than passes.\n\nVerified rather than assumed: git diff --check is clean; make vet passes; make test passes over 12 packages, unchanged, because the change is prose only; the worktree is clean at the exact head; and task/deployment-story still merges cleanly into current main by git merge-tree --write-tree against main edb53ce. No merge, no head movement on main, and no supersession of the round-17 artifact for this path.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2be2e2b14d26002b09148733722cd27092e73230","branch":"task/deployment-story","conditions":"F1 closed by removing the contract field from the activation body; F2 closed by a stated order of classification with identity=none and wrong-ref forms, both retained; F3 c